{
  "datasets": [
    {
      "name": "corridor_util",
      "displayName": "Corridor utilization (mv_corridor_utilization)",
      "asset_name": "cdm_tmforum.network_scenario_twin.mv_corridor_utilization"
    },
    {
      "name": "sla_exposure",
      "displayName": "SLA exposure at risk (mv_sla_exposure)",
      "asset_name": "cdm_tmforum.network_scenario_twin.mv_sla_exposure"
    },
    {
      "name": "copper_readiness",
      "displayName": "Copper decommissioning readiness (mv_copper_readiness)",
      "asset_name": "cdm_tmforum.network_scenario_twin.mv_copper_readiness"
    },
    {
      "name": "sla_span_status",
      "displayName": "SLA exposure by span with simulation status",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT resource_id, corridor_name, srlg, sim_id, next_window_id,\n",
        "  CASE WHEN sim_id IS NULL THEN 'No simulated result yet' ELSE 'Simulated' END AS sim_status,\n",
        "  MEASURE(sla_exposure_mrr) AS sla_exposure_mrr,\n",
        "  MEASURE(affected_customers) AS affected_customers,\n",
        "  MEASURE(dual_path_both_failed_customers) AS dual_path_both_failed_customers\n",
        "FROM cdm_tmforum.network_scenario_twin.mv_sla_exposure\n",
        "WHERE resource_type = 'span'\n",
        "GROUP BY ALL\n",
        "ORDER BY sla_exposure_mrr DESC NULLS LAST, resource_id"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "pages": [
    {
      "name": "overview",
      "displayName": "Network risk overview",
      "layout": [
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "header_text",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "## Lakelink Fiber Network Scenario Twin\n",
                "\n",
                "The intelligence layer above the inventory system of record, not an inventory system. Demo window Aug 18 to Nov 16, 2026 (synthetic data).\n",
                "\n",
                "Provenance: **Observed** = telemetry and gold tables, **Simulated** = blast-radius results, **Forecast** = capacity forecast. Units: money in USD/month, utilization in %, durations in days. A span without a simulation shows \"No simulated result yet\", never 0. Use Ask Genie for follow-up questions."
              ]
            }
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "width": 12,
            "height": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "kpi_denslc_days",
            "queries": [
              {
                "name": "main",
                "query": {
                  "datasetName": "corridor_util",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "days_to_exhaustion",
                      "expression": "MEASURE(`min_days_to_exhaustion`)"
                    }
                  ],
                  "filters": [
                    {
                      "expression": "`corridor_id` IN ('DEN-SLC')"
                    }
                  ],
                  "disaggregated": false
                }
              }
            ],
            "spec": {
              "version": 2,
              "widgetType": "counter",
              "frame": {
                "title": "DEN-SLC days to 95% exhaustion (Forecast)",
                "showTitle": true,
                "description": "Forecast exhaustion Mar 16, 2027; pre-build trigger 90 days earlier",
                "showDescription": true
              },
              "encodings": {
                "value": {
                  "fieldName": "days_to_exhaustion",
                  "displayName": "Days to exhaustion",
                  "format": {
                    "type": "number-plain",
                    "abbreviation": "none",
                    "decimalPlaces": {
                      "type": "max",
                      "places": 0
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "data": {
                "queryName": "main"
              }
            }
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 2,
            "width": 3,
            "height": 3
